# AVM pilot preflight — A_core vs C1

Isolated retrospective eligibility analysis. No Oracle/network, database, source
ingestion, productive identity, valuation, model training, prediction or predictive
metrics. The original 791-row cohort and certified harness remain immutable.

Reproduce from the workspace root (Windows, same user for DPAPI):

```powershell
& work/avm-01-20261008/.venv-repro/Scripts/python.exe -B research/tasar_pilot_preflight_20261010T123500Z/preflight.py verify
& work/avm-01-20261008/.venv-repro/Scripts/python.exe -B research/tasar_pilot_preflight_20261010T123500Z/test_preflight.py
```

`run` generates once and refuses overwrites; `verify` recalculates in memory and
compares all eight CSV files byte-for-byte. Originals are hash-checked before and
after. Read `manifest.json` for the frozen policy, hashes, versions, decision,
residual risks and test results. CSVs are UTF-8 and locally ignored by Git.

Identity review is automatic, price-blind and **not human certification**. Full
URLs are opaque equality identifiers because their slugs may contain prices.
Titles/descriptions are sanitized. Images are origin URL identifiers, not content
hashes. Source precision labels remain unverified. Different broker codes are not
unit identity. No old property_id/fingerprint is used to form CV groups.

G3 adds only plausible indeterminate pairs with specific local/name corroboration;
generic commune/floorplan/title templates remain unresolved, not certified
independent. Components include all 6283 snapshot nodes before eligibility and
audit every transitive component for positive conflicts. Additional high-risk
candidates are separate. The price-blind scan found **4211/4486**, both declaring
Avenida Macul 2470, with a 10% area difference outside the original candidate
band. Explicit policy **v2** conservatively cofolds this additional indeterminate
pair in G3, with no claim of unit identity. It remains separately disclosed in
`unresolved_identity_cases.csv`; the original 28 and original policy are untouched.
Any further high-risk candidate without disposition would block execution.

Legacy history aliases are linked only by exact source/external_id. Neither legacy
history nor modern observations enter the training pool. Row-level modern History
is unavailable locally: its identity completeness is **not certified**. This
design supports only retrospective Oct4 snapshot CV, not temporal forecasting.

The previous 711–716 figure was already fold-local, but an upper bound. This run
uses the actual ordered canonical dedup/structural/training-price/product/robust
filters. It reads monetary values **only from authorized training DTOs**, in memory,
after freezing identity/group/fold policy. Held target labels are never requested.
No monetary diagnostic is exported. Eligibility stops before ranking, aggregation
and surface adjustment. Counts at an early failure are the remaining pool at the
failed stage, not a prediction. Coverage is eligibility, not operational success.

C1 uses the actual certified nine-column matrix for the unchanged six features.
Median imputation/scaling/one-hot training scope and missing-prediction handling are
checked against the immutable code, not fitted on real data. Unknown categories
are allowed by `handle_unknown=ignore`; input processability does not certify
prediction coverage. Keep all 791 rows for future full-universe coverage and paired
errors on the common predicted subset. No holdout or official split is created.

Readiness never authorizes training by itself; the harness real-execution guard
remains unchanged. Residual cross-source recall and same-building dependence must
qualify any future exploratory conclusions; this is not a confirmatory benchmark.

Final review: **READY_FOR_EXPLORATORY_PILOT**, 36 tests passed / 0 failed; eight CSVs
reproduced byte-for-byte in a new process. G1/G2: 791 groups; G3: 781 groups
(772 singletons, 9 multiple groups, maximum cohort size 3, 1 cross-source group).
Primary G3 A eligibility: 702/791 (88.75%), 89 potential abstentions; predefined
seed range 702–710. C1 input processability: 791/791; no prediction coverage claim.
Portal A support 405/406 versus Yapo 297/385 materially limits paired-result scope.
A raw/stored geocode-precision discrepancy for listing4813 has no coordinates and
remains untrusted; it changes no identity or eligibility result.
The sole next action is authorization of a controlled exploratory retrospective
A_core vs C1 pilot with G3. The real-data execution guard remains unchanged.
